@meta
id: 17-17
title: Scenario — refunds need a reason
chapter: 17
type: scenario
skills: jumplist, marks-set, marks-jump, mark-backtick, search-slash, op-motion
par: 300
minutes: 15
vscode: four tabs, a lot of Ctrl+Tab, and Go to Definition when the language server is awake
open: order.provider.ts payment.service.ts order.entity.ts order.resolver.ts default.json
vimrc: set hidden

@brief
A ticket, not an exercise.

    PAY-207  Finance's export needs a reason against every refund.
             Thread a `reason` string from the GraphQL mutation down
             to the payment gateway, and store it on the order.

Five files are open as buffers. Four change; one does not.

  1. order.provider.ts — `cancel` takes `reason: string` as a second
     parameter, passes it as the second argument to
     `paymentService.refund`, and adds `refundReason: reason` to the
     update values after `status: 'CANCELLED'`.

  2. payment.service.ts — `refund` takes `reason: string` as a second
     parameter and sends it in the request body: `{ orderId, reason }`.

  3. order.entity.ts — `Order` gains `refundReason?: string;` under
     `cancellationReason?`.

  4. order.resolver.ts — `cancelOrder` accepts `reason: string` in its
     args type, after `id: string`, and passes `args.reason` to the
     provider.

  5. default.json — already has every code you need. Leave it alone.

Start in the provider, on the refund call. You will be leaving it for
the service and coming back to it, and the whole of this chapter has
been about doing that without searching twice. Every file except the
JSON is graded.

@keys
| `mA` `` `A `` | global mark, and back to it from any file |
| `Ctrl-O` | back through the jumplist, across files |
| `:b name` | switch to the buffer whose name contains `name` |
| `f)` `t}` | onto the paren, up to before the brace |
| `:wqa` | write everything, quit |

@hints
Do the provider's signature and the refund call together, then mark
the refund line before leaving for the service, since the update
values you still have to edit are just below it.
--
In the service, `/refund(` from the top of the file finds the
signature. The body's `{ orderId }` is the next line: `j` then `t}`.
--
Back in the provider, `/CANCELLED` and `t}` get you to the update
values. Then the entity and the resolver are one insert each, and the
resolver's second edit is on the line below its first; `0` before
`f)` because `j` keeps the column you ended the insert on.
--
Par assumes each new piece of text is typed exactly once and no line
is ever retyped. Roughly two hundred and sixty keystrokes, most of
them the new code.

@solution
One route, buffer by buffer.

**order.provider.ts** — `/cancel(` Enter, `f)i, reason: string` Esc.
`/refund(` Enter, `mA`, `f)i, reason` Esc.

**payment.service.ts** — `:b payment`. `/refund(` Enter,
`f)i, reason: string` Esc, `j` `t}i, reason` Esc.

**order.provider.ts again** — `` `A ``. `/CANCELLED` Enter,
`t}i, refundReason: reason` Esc.

**order.entity.ts** — `:b entity`. `/cancellationReason` Enter,
`orefundReason?: string;` Esc.

**order.resolver.ts** — `:b resolver`. `/cancelOrder` Enter,
`t}i; reason: string` Esc, `j` `0f)i, args.reason` Esc.

`:wqa`.

Nothing in this ticket is hard. The point is how much of it is
*navigation* rather than editing: nine jumps across four files, and
the code you typed is a handful of short inserts. In VS Code you
would have done it with tabs and the mouse and it would have taken
about as long. The difference is that this route never loses its
place, because every departure from a line was paired with a way
back that does not depend on remembering where you were.

`` `A `` was the right key for the return to the provider because you
had made two jumps inside the service and were not going to count
them. `Ctrl-O` twice would have done the same. Either is fine; what is
not fine is `:b provider` followed by scrolling.

The JSON file is there to be left alone, and to notice that `:b
default` is never typed. Buffers you do not touch cost nothing.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string, reason: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id, reason);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED', refundReason: reason },
    });
  }
}

@start payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/refunds`, { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@expected payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string, reason: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/refunds`, { orderId, reason });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@start order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@expected order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  cancellationReason?: string;
  refundReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@start order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

@expected order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string; reason: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id, args.reason);
  }
}

